ass=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Posidipp.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">12.4</span> </span>: c. dupl. acc., <span class=\"gk\">β. τὴν πόλιν τοὺς ὑπολοίπους</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">rob</b> her of.., <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">App.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">BC</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">2.131</span> </span>:—<span class=\"lex-gram\"> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Pass.</span> </span>, <span class=\"gk\">τοσούσδε βλαβῆναι τὴν πόλιν</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">lose</b> them, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Hann.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">28</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">τὸ βλαβέν,</span> = βλάβη, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Lg.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">933e</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"3\"><span class=\"lex-n\">2</span> c. acc. rei, <span class=\"gk\">β. λόγον</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">mar</b> the prophecy, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pi.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">P.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">9.94</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">τοὺς ὅρκους</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">violate</b> them, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Arist.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Fr.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">148</span> </span>. (<span class=\"gk\">βλαπ-&lt; μλαπ-</span> (<b class=\"lex-tr\">mḷq[uglide]</b>), cf. Skt. <b class=\"lex-tr\">marcáyati</b> 'injure', <b class=\"lex-tr\">mṛktás</b> 'wounded', Lat. <b class=\"lex-tr\">mulco</b> 'maltreat'.)</div></div>"}